The sun has come up and I am sitting by a window that is foggy with the breath of a life gone by. I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
m a sight this morning: two shirts, heavy pants, a scarf wrapped twice around my neck and tucked into a thick sweater knitted by my daughter thirty birthda\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37 
ys ago. The thermostat in my room is set as high as it will go, and a smaller space heater sits directly behind me. It clicks and groans and spews hot air like a fairy-tale dragon, and still my body shivers with a cold that will never go away, a cold that
\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37  h\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37 as been eighty years in the making. Eighty years, I think sometimes, and despite my own acceptance of my age, it still amazes me that I haven\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
t been warm since George Bush was president. I wonder if this is how it is for everyone my age.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid3364318 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2756734 \hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37 My life? It isn\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
t easy to explain. It has not been the rip-roaring spectacular I fancied it would be, but neither have I burrowed around with the gophers. I suppose it has most resembled a blue-chip stock: fairly stable, more ups than downs, and gradually
\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37  trending upward over time. A good buy, a lucky buy, and I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 
ve learned that not everyone can say this about his life. But do not be misled. I am nothing special; of this I am sure. I am a common man with common thoughts, and I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 ve led a common life. There a\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37 re
\hich\af37\dbch\af37\loch\f37  no monuments dedicated to me and my name will soon be forgotten, but I\hich\f37 \rquote \loch\f37 ve loved another with all my heart and soul, and to me, this has always been enough.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af37 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid3364318 
